# Blender addon updater scratch space.
# The CGCookie updater backs up the current addon, downloads the release zip and
# extracts it - all inside the addon folder. On a DEV install (Blender's addon
# symlinked to blender_plugin/) that lands in the working tree: ~260MB of
# backups, an extracted copy of the whole repo, and a ~47MB source.zip. Worse,
# each run backs up the PREVIOUS run's scratch, so it nests.
# The folder is named after updater.addon, which has already changed twice
# (bp_updater -> blender_plugin_updater -> animlib_updater), so match the
# suffix rather than any one name.
blender_plugin/*_updater/

# Filenames that are actually a broken shell command.
# A quoting slip turns `mkdir "...dir" && cp a b` into a single file literally
# named `dir" && cp a b`. It has happened twice here (two stale theme copies,
# and a pair in the addon folder), and it spreads by copying a folder between
# the private and public repos. Windows stores the illegal characters as
# private-use codepoints (U+F022 for `"`, U+F03A for `:`), so match the ASCII
# ` && ` that survives in the name instead.
* && *
